C("A French toggle record is one ASCII digit, colon, and exactly activé or désactivé, lowercase with precomposed accents. No whitespace or normalization.",r"[0-9]:(?:activé|désactivé)","0:activé|9:désactivé|1:activé|2:désactivé|3:activé|4:désactivé|5:activé|6:désactivé","0:Activé|0:desactivé|0:activé|0:désactivé|00:activé|a:activé|0:ACTIVÉ|0: activé","Precomposed accents and the one-digit prefix are exact.")
C("A city key is 2 through 8 Unicode letters only. No spaces, digits, marks or punctuation; length counts code points.",r"\p{L}{2,8}","ab|Été|東京|Δέλτα|مرحبا|Зима|abcdefgh|Aé","a|abcdefghi|ab1|a_b|a b|é|😀a","A Unicode letter class is broader than ASCII but excludes marks.","u")
C("A numeric glyph field is exactly four Unicode decimal digits, from any script; mixing scripts is allowed. No signs, spaces or other number categories.",r"\p{Nd}{4}","0000|9999|１２３４|١٢٣٤|१२३४|০১২৩|1٢３४|۴۵۶۷","123|12345|1a34|12 4|ⅣⅢⅡⅠ|²³⁴⁵|+123","Decimal digits differ from the entire Unicode number category.","u")
C("A Greek label is exactly three code points, each both a Unicode letter and in the Greek script. Marks and punctuation are forbidden.",r"(?:(?=\p{L})\p{Script=Greek}){3}","αβγ|ΑΒΓ|Δέλ|Ωωα|πστ|ήθο|ξψζ|κλμ","αβ|αβγδ|aβγ|α1γ|άβ|α·γ|αβ!","Script membership alone also contains nonletters.","u")
C("A Han tag is han: followed by exactly two Unicode letters in the Han script. No spaces, marks or punctuation.",r"han:(?:(?=\p{L})\p{Script=Han}){2}","han:東京|han:中文|han:漢字|han:山水|han:天地|han:日月|han:人心|han:大小","han:東|han:東京京|han:東a|han:あい|han:东1|Han:東京|han:東!","Both letter category and Han script are required.","u")
C("An international personal label contains 2 through 12 letter clusters. Each cluster is one Unicode letter followed by zero to two Unicode combining marks. No spaces, initial marks, digits or punctuation; count clusters rather than code points.",r"(?:\p{L}\p{M}{0,2}){2,12}","ab|éx|á̈b|Été|東京|Δέλτα|مرحبا|abcdefghijkl","a|abcdefghijklm|́ab|á̈̃b|ab1|a b|😀a","Marks must attach to a preceding letter and have a bounded count.","u")
C("A Latin locale label has 3 through 10 code points, each both a Unicode letter and in the Latin script. No marks, digits or whitespace.",r"(?:(?=\p{L})\p{Script=Latin}){3,10}","abc|Été|Straße|Ångström|abcdefghij|naïve|España|Łódź","ab|abcdefghijk|abα|ab1|éx|a b|ab😀","Latin script includes more than ASCII but script and category must intersect.","u")
C("An Arabic-digit reading is ar: followed by exactly four Arabic-Indic digits U+0660 through U+0669. Western, extended Arabic-Indic and other script digits are forbidden.",r"ar:[\u0660-\u0669]{4}","ar:٠٠٠٠|ar:٩٩٩٩|ar:١٢٣٤|ar:٤٣٢١|ar:١٠٠٠|ar:٠٠٠١|ar:٥٥٥٥|ar:٩٨٧٦","ar:٠٠٠|ar:٠٠٠٠٠|ar:1234|ar:۱۲۳۴|ar:١٢3٤|AR:١٢٣٤|ar:١٢a٤","Decimal-digit categories would accept scripts this field forbids.","u")
C("An international username is 4 through 12 Unicode code points, starts with a Unicode letter and then uses Unicode letters or ASCII digits. It must contain at least one ASCII digit; no combining marks or other digits.",r"(?=.{4,12}$)(?=.*[0-9])\p{L}[\p{L}0-9]*","abc1|Été2|東京12|Δέλτα3|مرحبا4|Зима5|abcdefghijk1|Aé12","abc|abcdefghijklm1|1abc|abcdef|abc١|ab́1|ab_1","Length uses code points; allowed digits remain ASCII.","u")
C("A Unicode heading is 4 through 16 code points consisting only of Unicode letters and ASCII spaces. It begins and ends with a letter and permits only single internal spaces; at least one space is required. Marks are forbidden.",r"(?=.{4,16}$)\p{L}+(?: \p{L}+)+","a bc|Été été|東京 大阪|Δέλτα Άλφα|مرحبا عالم|Зима лето|abcdefgh ijklmno|ab cd","abc|abcd|abcdefghijklmnopq| ab cd|ab cd |ab  cd|ab 1c|é ab","Space presence and placement interact with code-point length.","u")
